.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1033 AM PDT Fri Sep 25 2026

A mix of VFR-MVFR conditions this morning will give way to VFR
regionwide by this afternoon. High confidence for breezy onshore
winds this afternoon in wake of a dry frontal passage. Winds are
forecast to ease overnight and more so into early Saturday
morning. Low to moderate confidence for the return of low ceilings
and/or fog across the region early Saturday morning. The greatest
potential for sub-VFR conditions are at HAF, OAK, and SNS. Any
low clouds and/or fog will dissipate by 18Z Saturday.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Increasing west to northwest winds this
afternoon with gusts up to 28 kt. Low confidence for sub-VFR
conditions early Saturday morning through about 17Z with the
greatest potential over OAK. Winds ease early Saturday morning
before increasing once again in the afternoon with VFR conditions
likely to prevail throughout the day on Saturday.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Expecting increasing northwesterly
winds this afternoon before easing after sunset. The greatest
potential for sub-IFR conditions will be over SNS with the
potential for fog development, however have just SCT006 in at MRY
from 1100Z-1630Z Saturday to account for the uncertainty.


