.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 430 AM PDT Fri Sep 25 2026

Transition day across the district as a weak dry cold front sweeps
through. As of this writing the front is just pushing through the
N Bay and will traverse through the Central Coast by this
afternoon. The passing front will kick off a cooling and
moistening trend, which will continue through the weekend. More
importantly for a fire weather standpoint the passing front will
cause an uptick in winds. Winds will likely be strongest later
this afternoon and this evening. Winds ease overnight, but a weak
offshore push develops for early Saturday morning. Nothing to be
alarmed over as it will be weak and mainly N and E Bay higher
terrain.

